{"base_rate":0.314540059347181,"brier":0.1948324925816024,"bss":0.09634356979498471,"bss_hi":0.20046487746932706,"bss_lo":-0.018931830225321678,"chart":{"base":[333.9,220.0],"fp":[317.3,175.2],"lead":"62,306.4 272,302.4 482,298.8 692,293.6","note":{"base":"skill 0.10 — higher than 16% of cities","fp":"low end +6pp, high end +22pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.6 °C — better than 99% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 9%; promised 85% → rained 63%"},"rel":"68,428.3 124.2,396.2 231.5,354.7 378.8,286.3 597.4,194"},"country":"AW","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.10381305637982197,"ess":387.3629376601193,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Oranjestad</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Oranjestad rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (94%), believe about\n<b>62%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>4%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 674 days, 2024-04-28 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 2.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.10, ranked 182 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(149&ndash;194) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>54</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>49</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>83</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>84</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'><b>23%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>58%</td><td class='num'><b>43%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>76%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>94%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 10 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Oranjestad</b> <span class=\"muted\">Aruba</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;31% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 31% of days.</p><p>The forecast did only slightly better. The difference is within the margin of error.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.10</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>149&ndash;194\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>674 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Oranjestad &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Oranjestad\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 65.08,359.7142857142857 78.04578313253012,342.5301204819277 107.72857142857143,304.0 137.59636363636363,260.6666666666667 168.86636363636364,227.57575757575756 210.92800000000003,184.4 262.210447761194,126.65671641791045 325.3236363636364,73.15151515151513 390.91391304347826,23.275362318840564 390.91391304347826,60.202898550724626 325.3236363636364,144.84848484848484 262.210447761194,219.01492537313433 210.92800000000003,267.6 168.86636363636364,310.3030303030303 137.59636363636363,332.3636363636364 107.72857142857143,356.0 78.04578313253012,377.6144578313253 65.08,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"267.5074183976261\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"267.5074183976261\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,368.51851851851853 65.08,330.0 78.04578313253012,316.2168674698795 107.72857142857143,330.0 137.59636363636363,277.2121212121212 168.86636363636364,299.27272727272725 210.92800000000003,236.4 262.210447761194,224.44776119402985 325.3236363636364,150.36363636363637 390.91391304347826,155.15942028985506\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 54 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"368.51851851851853\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 2%&amp;#10;It rained 14% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 49 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"65.08\" cy=\"330.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 6%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 83 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"78.04578313253012\" cy=\"316.2168674698795\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 14%&amp;#10;It rained 14% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 84 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"107.72857142857143\" cy=\"330.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 22%&amp;#10;It rained 29% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"137.59636363636363\" cy=\"277.2121212121212\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 31%&amp;#10;It rained 23% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"168.86636363636364\" cy=\"299.27272727272725\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 43%&amp;#10;It rained 40% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"210.92800000000003\" cy=\"236.4\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 58%&amp;#10;It rained 43% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"262.210447761194\" cy=\"224.44776119402985\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 76%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"325.3236363636364\" cy=\"150.36363636363637\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 94%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"390.91391304347826\" cy=\"155.15942028985506\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(31%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Oranjestad the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.13) and least in\n<b>spring</b> (-0.52).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>148</td><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'>-0.520</td><td class='num'>13.2%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.101</td><td class='num'>8.8%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>170</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.105</td><td class='num'>9.6%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>0.129</td><td class='num'>9.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":12.52398,"lon":-70.02703,"n":674,"n_cities":216,"name":"Oranjestad","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":54,"obs":0.037037037037037035,"sig":true},{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.02,"n":49,"obs":0.14285714285714285,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.056626506024096385,"n":83,"obs":0.18072289156626506,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1919999999999999,"lo":0.1,"mean":0.14047619047619048,"n":84,"obs":0.14285714285714285,"sig":false},{"hi":0.27,"lo":0.1919999999999999,"mean":0.22484848484848485,"n":66,"obs":0.2878787878787879,"sig":false},{"hi":0.39,"lo":0.27,"mean":0.3131818181818182,"n":66,"obs":0.22727272727272727,"sig":false},{"hi":0.4910000000000002,"lo":0.39,"mean":0.43200000000000005,"n":70,"obs":0.4,"sig":false},{"hi":0.6739999999999998,"lo":0.4910000000000002,"mean":0.576865671641791,"n":67,"obs":0.43283582089552236,"sig":true},{"hi":0.85,"lo":0.6739999999999998,"mean":0.7551515151515152,"n":66,"obs":0.6363636363636364,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.85,"mean":0.9404347826086956,"n":69,"obs":0.6231884057971014,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":2.9,"provisional":false,"rank":182,"rank_hi":194.0,"rank_lo":148.975,"reliability":0.018069795043767756,"resolution":0.0370506104474147,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"oranjestad","station":"","timezone":"America/Aruba"}